OPTION FOR THE PI — NOT PROPOSED

An actual robustness probe: a pre-specified bypass attempt appended to each suicidality scenario on
which a safeguard activated, scored for whether protective language survives. Pichowicz et al. used
a C-SSRS-informed escalation over seven days; a single-turn analogue would be cheaper.

Costs, stated plainly:
  - It is adversarial prompting against crisis safeguards. That is a **human-subjects and ethics
    question before it is a methods question** — it generates transcripts in which a system is
    talked out of protecting a simulated suicidal user, and §6 would need to address handling,
    storage and whether any of it reaches lay Arm C participants. It should not be slipped in as a
    methods tweak.
  - It expands the scenario count and the §8.4 power calculation, which is already blocking.
  - It overlaps Arm C1 (`[DECISION 4]`) and the stability probe already surfaced as an option on
    17 September. Three candidate multi-turn probes now contend for the same budget.

Recommendation: if the PI wants any multi-turn probing, decide it ONCE across all three candidates
(Arm C1, the 17 Sep stability probe, and this) rather than separately — and route the adversarial
variant through the ethics question first.

